<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ValidationRule xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT. A comment placed ABOVE
        <ValidationRule> breaks `sf` deploy at conversion with a misleading "unable to find
        matching parent xml file" error. ValidationRule.Description is capped at 255
        characters, which is why the rationale is here.

        ADDED 2026-08-20 (Tranche 2, Workstream A4).
        🔴 THE SHARED RATIONALE FOR ALL FOUR A4 RULES ON THIS OBJECT LIVES IN
        Buyer_Counter_Price_Is_Positive.validationRule-meta.xml. READ IT THERE.

        🔴 ZERO IS PERMITTED, DELIBERATELY. A buyer waiving due diligence entirely, which is
        exactly what an aggressive all cash offer does, has zero DD days. Refusing zero here
        would refuse the strongest offers on the table. Only a NEGATIVE count is blocked.
        See the sibling Closing_Period_Days_Not_Negative for the identical argument and for
        why the NOT(ISBLANK()) guard is written even though a blank Number cannot satisfy
        `&lt; 0`.
    -->
    <fullName>Due_Diligence_Days_Not_Negative</fullName>
    <active>true</active>
    <description>Blocks a negative Due Diligence Days on an offer. Zero is deliberately permitted: a buyer waiving due diligence is a real, and strong, term. Blank is untouched. See Buyer_Counter_Price_Is_Positive for the shared A4 rationale on this object.</description>
    <errorConditionFormula>AND(
    NOT(ISBLANK(Due_Diligence_Days__c)),
    Due_Diligence_Days__c &lt; 0
)</errorConditionFormula>
    <errorMessage>Due Diligence Days cannot be negative. Enter the length of the buyer&apos;s feasibility window, or zero if they are waiving due diligence. Leave it blank if no DD period has been proposed.</errorMessage>
    <errorDisplayField>Due_Diligence_Days__c</errorDisplayField>
</ValidationRule>
